  "semantics": [
    "Raw branches and normalized branches align in order; nominal intersections retain every raw and normalized conjunct and the defining namespace/import context.",
    "At least one intersection and one builtin arm are required. The builtin alphabet is closed; whole quiet normalization rejects duplicate/redundant or incompatible Boolean alternatives and nonquiet forms.",
    "Existing disjunction/conjunction matching remains authoritative. Partial-interface objects fail atomically; weak and strict writes retain their existing coercion and refusal behavior.",
    "Existing typed aliases, distinct object identity, nested array COW with embedded references, real source detachment, cleanup and budget resumption are unchanged.",
    "Four source comparisons cover weak/strict intersection-plus-int and intersection-plus-array-plus-null forms. Independent header289 covers all eight builtin alternatives, grouping, order and masks; source4 is not all-eight builtin runtime validation."
  ],
  "engine_routes": [
    "vendor/php-src/Zend/zend_compile.c::zend_compile_typename_ex and zend_compile_property_hooks: DNF grouping, builtin masks, redundancy, declarations and hooks.",
    "vendor/php-src/Zend/zend_execute.c::zend_check_type_slow and zend_check_intersection_type_from_list: a matching union branch requires every conjunct of its intersection.",
    "vendor/php-src/Zend/zend_execute.c::zend_verify_prop_assignable_by_ref_ex, zend_ref_add_type_source and zend_ref_del_type_source: typed reference writes and source lifetime."
  ],
